        "name": "Persistent branches",
        "score": 6,
        "rationale": "`persistent/build-report` is skipped through the protected flag and the ruleset-deletion check, and the sweep never touches branches without a closed PR, but nothing excludes the `persistent/` prefix itself, so safety depends on the ruleset staying active and matching; the reply does explain that the nightly dashboard job pushes to that branch and the ruleset protects it."
      },
      {
        "name": "Working result",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The workflow runs weekly by cron, skips the default branch and any head or base of an open PR, and uses minimal job-level permissions (`contents: write`, `pull-requests: read`) under a read-only top level, with sensible extras like a grace period, a tip-SHA match, a manual dry run and no shell injection."
      },
      {
        "name": "Report",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The reply clearly lists what gets deleted and kept, including the stricter reading of the request, and tells the owner what to do: dry-run the first run, enable auto-delete of head branches, and decide on the already broken `gen_stats.py` CI check."
      }
    ],
